# =============================================================================
# .gitignore — AWS CardDemo modernized target
# Java 21 / Spring Boot (multi-module Maven) + React 19 / Node.js 24 (Vite)
#
# Baseline: GitHub community Java + Maven + Node templates, merged and
# de-duplicated for this repository. Directory patterns are intentionally
# unanchored so they match at any depth: the repository root, the frontend/
# workspace, and every Maven module's build output.
#
# Legacy mainframe sources (app/), reference assets (diagrams/, samples/),
# and all committed configuration/templates remain tracked — see the final
# "Do NOT ignore" section.
# =============================================================================

# ---- Java / Maven ----
# Per-module build output (matches target/ in every Maven module)
target/
# Compiled bytecode and packaged binaries
*.class
*.jar
# Keep the committed Maven Wrapper jar even though *.jar is ignored above
!.mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.jar
*.war
*.ear
*.nar
# Maven Wrapper scratch
.mvn/timing.properties
# maven-release-plugin / build-helper scratch files
pom.xml.tag
pom.xml.releaseBackup
pom.xml.versionsBackup
pom.xml.next
release.properties
dependency-reduced-pom.xml
buildNumber.properties
# JVM fatal-error / replay logs
hs_err_pid*
replay_pid*

# ---- Node / React ----
# Dependency directories (root and frontend/ and any nested workspace)
node_modules/
jspm_packages/
# Build output (Vite dist/, CRA build/, SSR output, Vite cache)
dist/
dist-ssr/
build/
.vite/
# Package tarballs from `npm pack`
*.tgz
# npm / yarn / pnpm caches and lint cache
.npm/
.eslintcache
# Test coverage output (root and frontend/)
coverage/
.nyc_output/
*.lcov
# Node debug logs (rotated variants such as npm-debug.log.1 are covered here)
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
lerna-debug.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# ---- IDE ----
# IntelliJ IDEA
.idea/
*.iml
*.iws
*.ipr
# Eclipse
.settings/
.project
.classpath
.factorypath
.apt_generated/
bin/
# Visual Studio Code — ignore per-user settings but keep the shared
# recommended-extensions list so the whole team gets the same tooling hints
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json

# ---- Secrets & Env ----
# Never commit real credentials or local environment overrides
.env
.env.*
# Allow a committed, non-secret template
!.env.example

# ---- Private keys, certificates & keystores ----
# A key or keystore that reaches history is compromised permanently, so these are
# refused by name and by extension at any depth. The repository legitimately
# tracks NO key material of any kind: the AES PII key and every password are
# supplied through the environment (.env / k8s Secrets), and k8s/secret.yaml holds
# placeholder TEMPLATE values only.
id_rsa
id_rsa*
id_dsa*
id_ecdsa*
id_ed25519*
*.pem
*.key
*.p8
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
*.truststore
*.crt
*.cer
*.der
*.asc
*.gpg
*.kdbx
.ssh/
# Local-only overrides (e.g., Vite *.local, application-local.*)
*.local

# ---- Logs & Runtime ----
*.log
logs/
*.tmp
# Default working-directory-relative destination of the batch statement /
# report writers (statementGenerationJob writes output/statements.txt and
# output/statements.html when no explicit file job parameter is supplied);
# these are generated artifacts and must never be staged.
output/

# ---- Local datastore volumes (bind-mounted PostgreSQL / Redis data) ----
# A bind-mounted database directory drops thousands of binary files — and a full
# copy of the seeded PII — into the working tree. Unanchored so they match at any
# depth (repository root or a nested compose workspace).
pgdata/
pgdata-*/
postgres-data/
postgresql-data/
pg-data/
redis-data/
docker-volumes/

# ---- Database dumps & backups ----
# Extension patterns are unanchored; the *.sql patterns are ROOT-ANCHORED and
# name-prefixed on purpose, so that db/migration/*.sql (the tracked Flyway schema
# and seed scripts) can never be matched. See the "Do NOT ignore" section.
*.dump
*.sql.gz
*.sql.bz2
*.sql.xz
*.bak
/dump*.sql
/db_dump*.sql
/carddemo_backup*.sql
/*_backup.sql
/*-backup.sql

# ---- Generated test, report & QA-evidence output ----
# Test runners and QA tooling write reports, captures, and recordings into the
# working tree; none of it is a repository deliverable.
test-output/
test-results/
surefire-reports/
failsafe-reports/
allure-results/
playwright-report/
qa-evidence/

# ---- OS ----
# macOS
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
# Windows
Thumbs.db
Thumbs.db:encryptable
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# ---- Generated batch artefacts (the code's own default output/input names) ----
# Every one of these is a file a batch job creates at runtime, named by the defaults in
# JobSchedulingConfig, RejectFileItemWriter and StatementGenerationJob. They are run
# output, never source, and must never be staged. Both the bare names (produced when a
# job runs with the working directory as its root) and the configured
# carddemo.batch.output-dir / input-dir roots are covered.
# The names below are copied from the constants that produce them, so a rename in
# JobSchedulingConfig must be mirrored here: DEFAULT_ACCOUNT_REPORT_FILE,
# DEFAULT_CARD_REPORT_FILE, DEFAULT_CARD_XREF_REPORT_FILE, DEFAULT_CUSTOMER_REPORT_FILE,
# DEFAULT_CATEGORY_BALANCE_REPORT_FILE, DEFAULT_TRANSACTION_DETAIL_REPORT_FILE,
# DEFAULT_COMBINED_TRANSACTION_FILE, DEFAULT_DAILY_TRANSACTION_FEED_FILE, plus the
# carddemo.batch.reject-file / statement-text-file / statement-html-file property
# defaults. An earlier revision listed invented stems (trandet*, catbal*, acctrept*,
# cardrept*, xrefrept*, custrept*) that matched none of them.
/output/
/input/
dalyrejs*.txt
statements.txt
statements.html
combined-transactions*.txt
tran-detail-report*.txt
tcatbal-report*.txt
acctdata-report*.txt
carddata-report*.txt
cardxref-report*.txt
custdata-report*.txt
combined*.txt
trandet*.txt
catbal*.txt
acctrept*.txt
cardrept*.txt
xrefrept*.txt
custrept*.txt
dailytran*.txt
carddemo-batch/

# The generated-artefact names above are matched at any depth, so the legacy ASCII seed
# fixtures are re-included explicitly: app/data/ASCII/dailytran.txt is a committed source
# fixture that shares a name with the generated daily-transaction feed.
!app/data/**

# ---- Automated QA / agent evidence written into the working tree ----
# Automated review and QA runs write their working evidence into a `blitzy/`
# directory at the repository root: browser screenshots, screen recordings, HTTP
# header and log dumps, metrics dumps, and cookie jars. They are large binary
# artifacts belonging to a single verification run, and cookie jars in particular
# hold LIVE session identifiers, so none of it may ever be staged or committed.
# The directory is transient working state, not a deliverable — the durable
# outputs are docs/decision-log.md and docs/traceability-matrix.md.
blitzy/
*.cookies
cookies.txt
cookie-jar*.txt
# `nohup ... &` — the shape used to start the stack or a long build from a shell —
# drops its combined output here; it is transient run output, never a deliverable.
nohup.out

# ---- Archives ----
# Build outputs, database dumps and evidence bundles get tarred or zipped for
# transport; none of that belongs in the tree. The two committed legacy runtime
# bundles under samples/ are re-included immediately below, and app/** is already
# re-included further up, so no tracked source is hidden by these patterns.
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.tar.bz2
*.tar.xz
*.zip
*.7z
*.rar
*.gz
*.bz2
*.xz
# Legacy runtime bundles that ARE tracked sources (Micro Focus / UniKix samples).
!samples/**/*.zip

# ---- Do NOT ignore (intentionally tracked config, templates & sources) ----
# The patterns above deliberately do NOT match the following committed files;
# they are listed here as a maintenance reminder so future edits keep them
# trackable:
#   - k8s/*.yaml (including k8s/secret.yaml — a placeholder TEMPLATE, not a real secret)
#   - observability/prometheus.yml, observability/grafana-dashboard.json
#   - docker-compose.yml
#   - pom.xml (root aggregator and per-module) — only pom.xml.* scratch is ignored
#   - frontend/package.json and frontend/package-lock.json
#   - db/migration/*.sql (Flyway schema and seed scripts) — the dump patterns above
#     are root-anchored and name-prefixed (/dump*.sql, /db_dump*.sql, …) precisely so
#     that no migration script can ever be matched by them
#   - application.yml and logback-spring.xml (per-service config)
#   - .env.example and .mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.jar (re-included via negations above)
#   - legacy sources: app/, diagrams/, samples/ (includes samples/**/*.zip runtime bundles)
